---
description: Keep Rust protocol boundaries strongly typed
globs: src/**/*.rs
alwaysApply: false
---

# Typed protocol DTOs

- Model stable JSON protocol messages, manifests, commands, results and runtime state with
  `Serialize` / `Deserialize` DTOs. Do not construct or inspect these contracts with
  `serde_json::Value`, `json!`, object indexing, or stringly-typed field maps.
- Use `serde_json::Value` only at an explicitly documented forward-compatible or untyped
  boundary where a closed DTO cannot represent the contract; validate and convert it immediately.
- Keep protocol field names, enum values, optional fields, bounds and unknown-field rejection in
  the DTO/serde declaration. Add a focused wire-shape test whenever a DTO changes.
- JSON values in test fixtures are allowed, but assertions for production wire shape should decode
  into the relevant DTO where practical.
